factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 7 problems
  reel_script says the government expressed concern about bar-related incidents; the article says the government ordered police to take urgent action, not that it 'கவலை தெரிவித்துள்ளது'
  reel_script says the police warned bar owners because of rising drug use among students, but the article only says drug use is rising; the link to the bar warning is an inference, and the reel's 'இதற்குக் காரணம்' presents it as established cause
  reel_script says 'உரிமதாரர்களுடன் கூட்டம் நடைபெற்றது' without the article's detail that the meeting was held at the commissioner's office with the 11 to 11 bar licensees and managers, and drops the arrest-free but key fact that licensees and managers were called in
  caption states 'நேற்று' (yesterday) for the meeting, which is consistent with the article, but the caption describes the warning as applying to 'எப்.எல்.2 மற்றும் எப்.எல்.3 பார்களுக்கு' while also calling 11 டு 11 bars 'அழைக்கப்படும்' without noting the article describes it as a common term; minor wording, but the caption also says drug sales target students which the article states, so this is acceptable
  reel_script states 'சீருடை அணிந்த மாணவர்கள் உள்ளே இருப்பது தெரிந்தால் அந்த பார் மீது உடனடி நடவடிக்கை' – article says 'உடனடி நடவடிக்கை எடுக்கப்படும' which matches, but the reel omits that the warning applies to students 'தனியாகவோ குழுவாகவோ' which is included; no issue here
  slides_spec hl2 says '18 வயதுக்குக் கீழ் அனுமதி' which reads as if admission under 18 is permitted, the opposite of the intended warning, making the headline ungrammatical in meaning
  reel_script and caption mention that the police cited social media invitations as the reason, but the reel attributes the bar warning to rising drug and alcohol use rather than the social-media-invitation information, mixing two separate causes into one claim
